WEBVTT

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.260
What the hell is going on?

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.930
The Kazanari Organization HQ
 has been annihilated?

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.170
Where are the others?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.810
Kirika-chan!

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.470
Hang in there, Maria!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.050
Maria!

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.210
I'm... alive...

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.120
We've lost.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:49.020
<b>Episode 5
Risking Your Life In A Fictional Warzone</b>

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.940
We've lost as badly as it's possible to lose.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:52.370
The controlling director of the 
Bavarian Illuminati finally appeared.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.550
Adam Weishaupt.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.250
And...

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:02.270
The Faust Robes of the Alchemists.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.180
When our blades crossed,

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.340
it felt like the Ignite's power 
was forcibly stripped from us.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.720
What was that force?

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:14.080
I believe it is the power of the 
Lapis Philosophicus, the Philosopher's Stone.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.790
The Philosopher's Stone...

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.550
The ultimate goal of the Alchemists' search 
for perfection, realized in physical form.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:29.230
It purges all impurities, 
including illness, burning them away.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:35.340
The Dáinsleif that forms the core of the 
Ignite Module had no hope against it.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:38.690
So, essentially, it's the 
Ignite's natural enemy.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.910
The force of the module 
being forcibly shut down

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.560
made me feel like
 I was being ripped apart.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:48.110
That thing's our ultimate weapon, 
but now it's a weakness?

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.120
Did the others arrive safely in Tokyo?

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:56.110
We'll have to wait for the full exam,

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.840
but, miraculously, they do not 
seem to have any major injuries.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.780
They'll be okay.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.770
Yes, you're right.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:08.050
They'll be fine. I know it.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.860
<i>Using their gears without a LiNKER,</i>

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.850
<i>plus the stress placed on 
their bodies by the Ignite Module...</i>

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:17.690
<i>The backlash could have been
 on the scale of a Climax Song...</i>

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.970
<i>But...</i>

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:26.400
The decision has been made to abandon 
the Kazanari Organization HQ.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.860
Everyone, prepare to leave.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:32.000
If we'd managed to decrypt 
the Valverde papers,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.400
there may have been
 something we could do...

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.220
Commander.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.950
Kamakura wants to see you.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.190
They're gonna give me one hell of a dressing down.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:03.570
The light of the Lapis overwhelmed 
the darkness of the Ignite.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:07.190
Our victory was assured. But...

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:12.400
We could've ended up burnt 
to a crisp ourselves!

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.130
And not only that, we didn't finish them off.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:24.770
Everybody, Adam is here!

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.230
Instead of being grumpy,
 let's be shiny instead!

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.780
Everybody!

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:33.360
Calm down, Tiki.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:37.020
But, you know, they're right.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:41.060
I joined the battle to show off.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.810
Since I was in the area...

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.010
But you know,

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:49.990
I think I'll let you handle the Symphogears.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.460
Controlling Director, where are you going?

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:57.410
Tiki read the stars and told me, right?

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.190
Yeah.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.340
The experiment was a success, right?

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:04.130
So let's do it for real next time.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.310
And manifest the power of a god.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:22.200
<i>Zeios Igalima raizen tron!</i>

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:59.970
<i>A happy-go-lucky girl from the depths 
of hell, scaring demons dead pale</i>

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:04.890
<i>Waving around my scythe around</i>

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.900
<b>Opposite Scythe Rapunzel</b>

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:09.420
The blades of Shul Shagana spin eternally, 
cutting a path through everything!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:16.240
<i>With my trademark cross and pointed cap</i>

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.460
Cutting through the 
obstacles in front of us,

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:14.010
and opening up our tomorrow!

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.160
<b>Δ Style Charming Axel Killer</b>

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:19.890
The Igalima can cut through anything.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.040
A ghost! A god!

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.660
It'll slice them in two!

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:30.010
<i>A melody of love that's 
just for the two of us</i>

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.870
Those girls keep pushing 
themselves too hard...

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:36.310
<i>What can I do to be a sun 
that protects the moon?</i>

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:34.030
Maria-san!

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:35.940
Should you be up?

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.590
You're not in great shape, either!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:41.650
<i>Shine brightly, sunshine, the two of us are one</i>

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:44.540
<i>Bring our bonds together with passion</i>

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:47.400
<i>Now let them overlap...</i>

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:53.220
Kiri-chan!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.240
Are you okay?

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.700
Shirabe-chan! Kirika-chan!

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.160
Why are you doing this without LiNKER?

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:15.510
If we had been able to fight 
without LiNKER, we could have...

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.580
But...

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:21.800
We're fine.

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:25.030
Let's keep training.

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:30.450
We need to increase our compatibility numbers, 
so we don't need to rely on the LiNKER.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:32.360
But this is crazy! You can't!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.190
One wrong move and you might die!

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:40.520
Your numbers are fine and
 you've never had to wonder why.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:41.870
You wouldn't understand!

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.760
Even if we don't die,

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:50.080
always being treated like leftovers is so 
painful that it feels like it'll kill us!

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:53.380
Let them do it.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.540
Maria-san!

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:58.880
I'll train with them and make 
sure they don't overdo it.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.680
You're not increasing their compatibility!

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.350
You're just adding to the 
number of idiots in the room!

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:06.100
One day, I know the LiNKER will be perfected.

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:14.030
But we don't have time
 to wait for that day.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.630
There's a way.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:21.450
A way that may create the last piece 
we need to finish the LiNKER.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.210
The last piece...

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:24.450
Really?

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:30.290
There is one part in the LiNKER recipe 
Dr. Ver gave me that I couldn't analyze.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:33.010
It's the place in the brain 
that the LiNKER connects to

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:37.930
in order to reduce the stress 
from the Symphogear.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.900
Even if he did have Finé 
and the FIS's help,

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.300
being able to create the LiNKER

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:47.980
means that he truly was a wonderful
 biologist, despite his many flaws.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:51.390
"Wonderful"? That's a terrifying thought.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:55.950
Um... let's fast forward 
over all the technobabble,

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.350
and just get to the part 
about the last piece.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:01.480
The key is Maria-san's Airgetlám.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:04.960
The silver... My gear?

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:10.270
One of the Airgetlám's special abilities 
is controlling energy vectors.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.530
The light we've seen several times 
when you were in dire peril...

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:17.460
That light was electrical signals
 going between the brain

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:20.160
and your Symphogear becoming 
visible thanks to the Airgetlám.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:25.350
I believe that it may have reduced the stress 
on the body from the Symphogear, as well.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:29.890
The training you've done 
between all your missions has,

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:34.300
little by little, raised your 
compatibility coefficient.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.430
I believe that is the result.

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:42.680
Maria's compatibility coefficient is 
the highest out of the three of us.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:43.680
And that means...

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.950
All of our hard work wasn't for nothing!

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:52.430
Yes. If we follow the electrical signal 
traces left in Maria-sama's brain...

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:55.670
We can find out what the LiNKER 
is having an effect on?

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.870
But how?

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:01.220
You'd have to go begging to 
that bastard Ver to find out.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:03.910
Follow me, please.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:06.800
What is this?

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:10.940
A present from Dr. Ver. 
The Direct Feedback System.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.900
I recreated it using applied alchemy.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.490
It turns the psyche of another person

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:20.300
into electrical signals and sends them 
into the user's brain to allow observation.

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:23.440
So you can use it to peek
 inside someone's head?

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.310
Theoretically.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:29.530
But the brain is a complex labyrinth.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.850
In the worst case, the minds of the observer 
and the subject may meld together,

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.640
destroying them both...

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:37.000
I'll do it.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.920
We've finally got a way 
to finish the LiNKER.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.500
There's no reason to let it go.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.310
But it's too dangerous!

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:45.980
You're being reckless!

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.840
Are you ones to talk?

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:56.600
So it poses a danger to the observer, that is to say, you, as well?

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:59.020
That's the battle that I can fight.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.990
Fight with me, please, Maria-san!

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:21.040
So you allowed a foreign enemy 
to trample on our soil?

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:25.450
And as a result, the Kazanari Organization's 
headquarters in Matsushiro was destroyed.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:30.270
We lost most of the secrets 
that we'd saved since the war.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:33.990
It is due to our own failure that 
this foreign threat came to our soil,

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:35.860
and we failed to drive it away.

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:37.410
Words cannot express our—

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:38.900
This isn't even worth listening to!

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:47.820
You understand, yes?

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:51.620
I will ensure that the law pertaining to 
national defense is quickly passed.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.820
You're not treating this with the 
seriousness it deserves. Do it now!

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:00.920
You're a failure as a protector.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:04.910
It is a shame that the blood of 
the Kazanari flows within you.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:10.650
I believe it is not our blood that 
makes us protectors, but our hearts.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.290
Shall we begin?

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:26.900
Yes. So you're coming inside my mind, right?

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:31.610
More precisely, I'm connecting to the structure 
of your brain, displayed in virtual reality.

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:34.770
Your consciousness and mine will be shared.

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:35.800
Understood.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.730
Kiri-chan, I know you're worried, but...

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:51.630
I know! I've made a fully informed decision!

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:57.380
That's what you get for eating something as 
adventurous as egg-flavored chocolate fish.

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:00.630
Make sure you finish your meal, normie.

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.320
It's good.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.240
This is for good luck!

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:10.700
If I can eat the whole thing, it means that 
what Maria and Elfnein are doing will work!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.610
Hibiki? Hey, Hibiki?

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:18.230
What?

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.330
It's melting.

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:29.980
At the very least, I can hear you out,
 or wipe that ice cream off your face.

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:33.420
So, when something happens, 
you can talk to me.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:37.600
Thank you, Miku. You really are my sunshine.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:41.940
Young Soccer Player With Missing Leg Comes to Japan For Surgery

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:39.190
<i>And now, our next story.</i>

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:42.900
<i>Stephan-kun, who lost his leg 
in a civil war back home,</i>

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:49.150
<i>has come from the Valverde Republic 
to get an advanced prosthetic,</i>

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:52.370
<i>so that he can once again play soccer.</i>

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:57.010
That's great, huh? 
He'll be able to play soccer again.

00:14:57.010 --> 00:14:58.710
I hope...

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:04.730
The fact that you suffered over a choice 
doesn't always mean it's the right one.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.680
In fact...

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:10.090
Sometimes there is no right choice at all.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.160
Are you ready? Here we go.

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:43.200
<i>The apple floated in the sky</i>

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:44.190
This is Maria's mind...

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:51.830
<i>the apple fell down to the ground.</i>

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.230
What's inside her heart, 
depicted by her memories...

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:56.350
<i>The stars were born</i>

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:56.220
Maria-san?

00:15:56.350 --> 00:16:00.770
<i>The songs were born</i>

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:03.430
Ow!

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.180
Why?

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:10.540
You're going to start combat training today.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:14.340
Receptor Children who could 
not become Finé's vessel

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:18.560
shall contribute to the organization not 
by shedding tears, but by shedding blood.

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:25.950
<i>Since I'm sharing her mind, her memories 
and experiences reach me as well.</i>

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.500
Where is it?

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:44.020
The part of the brain that
 connects with the gear...

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:57.790
Drink it. Now.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.680
<i>What's this? Memories of Noise?</i>

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:33.860
<i>If I die here, the real me 
probably won't wake up...</i>

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:54.200
<i>Seilien coffin Airgetlám tron...</i>

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:04.090
Maria-san?

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:09.240
Even if it's you, it's a little embarrassing 
having someone see my memories.

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:13.730
Um, when and what memory 
are you from, Maria-san?

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:16.740
We just promised to fight together, right?

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:21.490
If our minds are being shared, 
then you're not the only one who's here.

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:25.290
What's wrong with me 
kicking butt inside myself?

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:30.370
<i>How many times did I cry? 
How many times did I break?</i>

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:35.380
<i>It doesn't matter at all.</i>

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:33.890
This isn't a memory... 
it's Maria-san's mind!

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:36.120
We're breaking through!

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:37.260
Okay!

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:42.230
<i>There's no need for pride 
or fancy accessories</i>

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:47.130
<i>Let's reveal ourselves.</i>

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:48.970
What?

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:54.760
What is this place?

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:59.330
An image in your heart, from your memories 
that you've nearly forgotten, perhaps?

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:01.130
In my heart?

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:15.010
<i>How are the two of them doing?</i>

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:18.210
Their vitals are well below normal.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.740
If this state continues...

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:22.170
<i>We have no choice.</i>

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:25.040
We'll have to temporarily cancel...

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.600
What's wrong?

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.530
Alca-Noise have been spotted in Tokyo Bay!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:33.110
First, the one that could 
cut away part of space,

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.980
and now another new form...

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:37.790
And it seems quite sizable!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:39.790
We can't let it through...

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:40.900
I'm going!

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:55.140
The basement of that opera house was loaded 
with all kinds of things, not just Tiki.

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:58.170
We can't be holding back.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:01.300
Yes. The Bavarian Illuminati

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:06.380
will use the power of the gods to 
return the world to its proper state.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:09.560
If it's to help someone...

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:13.230
We can work together...

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:18.880
The greater justice... 
no, justice is on our side...

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:23.570
I will not turn back on this path,
even if I must ravel it alone.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.010
You're not alone.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:28.330
I won't let you be alone.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:31.800
We're here thanks to you.

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:34.260
The three of us will be together forever.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:43.340
<b>Designated Special Disaster Appears</b>

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:43.340
<b>Emergency Evacuation of Tokyo Bay</b>

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:42.730
Okay! We're heading to the helicopter point!

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:45.310
We can mope later!

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:46.170
Let's go!

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:48.900
We're heading to HQ!

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.360
I'm worried about the two of them!

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:57.230
Miku, get to the shelter in the school.

00:20:58.670 --> 00:20:59.770
Hibiki!

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:06.500
Everybody has something that 
they'll never give up on.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:11.020
But that doesn't mean I can't win.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:13.650
You don't have to win.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:20.580
But make sure you don't lose.

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:30.310
I have a song in my heart!

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:32.440
Yeah.

00:23:11.210 --> 00:23:12.180
Maria...

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:14.590
Maria...

00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:15.660
Wake up.

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:21.680
You're...

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:26.060
Indeed. I am a hero who's 
just passing through.

00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:29.090
Dr. Ver! I thought you were dead!

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:32.680
